A||||12||firstfiero||High velocity spinning in a 300z!||||1||
Z||000000||firstfiero||12-01-2001||12:37 PM||||     Last night at about 1 A.M. my friend showed up at the restraunt I manage in his 92 300z. He was driving like a maniac as usual  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and decided to go across the street to the empty grocery store parking lot and start doing 360 spins. It was pretty sweet. His engine was screaming and the tires were smokeing. Anyway when he got done he wanted me to take the fiero over and do the same. I love to fish tail but that really seemed like to much of a beating for my 16 year old car. I know I could have done them easily but what damage other then to tires can I expect? <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||avengador1||12-01-2001||12:40 PM||||I won't go there, but if you do and your car is not up to par, expect an expen$$ive repair bill for the part$$ that will break. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fierowrecker||12-01-2001||12:48 PM||||Depending on the state of disrepair your car is in, ball joints, tie-rods, etc...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||12-01-2001||01:07 PM||||Knew a guy who was doing something like that in a 74 Challenger 360. Till a lamp post jumped out in front of him. <BR>Gave him a bad day.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||12-01-2001||01:29 PM||||Fun stuff! I did a few double donuts in my 84 on thursday night. It was raining out and about midnight. I was at an intersection turning onto a dead road near my house. So I rev the engine to about 3K, drop the clutch, crank the wheel, and hold on. Went around 2 times one way, turned the wheel and went around about 4 times the other. Best part was when I decided I had enough. So I turn myself out of the spin and do a nice big fishtail for about 10-15feet into the correct direction.<P>In the rain I dont think it will hurt much. If it does... "Oh well". Gotta have fun sometimes.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> If I *really* abuse my clutch I'm sure I could get a donut or to out of my old duke on dry road. I don't think im going to try it anytime soon. Maybe if I had stock 14" wheels, but not with 16".<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 12-01-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||Jefrysuko||12-01-2001||02:27 PM||||When you feel like having a thrill just go and ride with him.  That way when something breaks you don't have to pay for it.||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||12-01-2001||03:46 PM||||     he wants me to but I like to be in controll when driving a little crazy. The parking lot was wet from the rain so I don't think I would have done much damage. My girl is in pretty good shape but 14 years on the same suspension parts means something will probobly give out.<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||12-01-2001||04:23 PM||||I did that when I showed up at my Friend's apartment last week.. parking lot was a little damp from rain.  Didn't realize I was laying rubber down till I smelled the tire smoke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Left some good marks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000008||BlackStang95||12-01-2001||06:48 PM||||I used to known as the donut king around here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> spektrum can vouch for it.  Other than a clutch and back tires I've never had to replace anything.  And I did a LOT of them.  I had power steering to worry about too.  I don't see you breaking anything that wouldnt give out soon under normal driving anyway.  have fun!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
